BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Katie Sanders: Ortiz’s War
DTSTART:20261021T003000Z
DTEND:20261021T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T122917Z
UID:51d21ad8-f944-5bf5-9d58-340db204e238
DESCRIPTION:Peter Ortiz’s path to becoming the most battle-decorated mem
 ber of America’s first spy agency—and one of the most decorated Marine
 s of World War II—was unlike any other. Born in New York and raised in b
 oth California and France\, he was a merchant seaman\, dude ranch manager
 \, race car driver\, lion tamer\, circus performer\, and Hollywood stuntma
 n and actor. As a teenager\, Ortiz ran away from boarding school to join t
 he French Foreign Legion. He fought in North Africa against Saharan tribes
 men\, and on the front lines against the Germans in 1940\, where he was ba
 dly wounded and captured.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealth
 club.org/events/2026-10-20/katie-sanders-ortizs-war
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Auditorium
 \, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-10-20/katie-sanders-ortiz
 s-war
END:VEVENT
